  "steps": [
    "Preheat the oven to 390°F (200°C; 355°F / 180°C fan).",
    "Toast the panko: Spread it on a baking tray, spray with oil (spray from above so the crumbs do not blow off), and bake 3-5 minutes until light golden. Transfer to a bowl.",
    "Set a rack on a baking tray; it helps the tenders bake evenly but is not essential.",
    "Whisk the batter ingredients with a fork until combined. Add the chicken and toss to coat.",
    "With tongs, lift each piece into the panko bowl, sprinkle crumbs over the top, and press to adhere. Transfer to the rack. Repeat with the rest.",
    "Spray lightly with oil and sprinkle with a touch of salt if you like. Bake 15 minutes, or up to 20 for very large pieces, until golden and 165°F inside. Longer dries them out.",
    "Serve right away with a dipping sauce (honey mustard works well) and a sprinkle of parsley."
